                  "explanation": "All three conditions — fever, acidemia, and hypercapnia — are classic right-shift triggers (CADET). The Bohr effect makes Hb release O₂ more readily at any given PO₂, which is exactly what the hypoxic tissues need. This is the body's compensation, not a defect. (Note: severe right shift also raises P50, so SpO₂ for the same PaO₂ may drop slightly.)",
